<title>CANADA: E Prairie grainbelt faces high frost risk Thursday.</title>
<headline>E Prairie grainbelt faces high frost risk Thursday.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The eastern half of Canada's Prairie grainbelt was forecast to see a high risk of frost Thusday morning, Environment Canada said.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was likely in Alberta's foothills and a slight risk was seen across the rest of Alberta and southwest Saskatchewan, Environment Canada said in its 10-day frost outlook.</p>
<p>A moderate risk of frost was forecast for north Alberta's grainbelt, northwest to southeast Saskatchewan and the extreme southwest of Manitoba Friday and Saturday mornings.</p>
<p>A high risk was seen on north, central grainbelt Oct 6, 7.</p>
</text>
